 "url": "issues/daily/2026/11/2026-11-16.html",
 "subject": "Macs will ask which apps an AI agent may control",
 "preview": "California takes OpenAI to court over its test agents, Google lets teams share Gemini skills, OpenAI's agents start working hospital software, and Tencent prices a model near zero.",
 "body": "<!-- buttondown-editor-mode: fancy -->\n<div style=\"display:none;max-height:0;overflow:hidden;mso-hide:all\">California takes OpenAI to court over its test agents, Google lets teams share Gemini skills, OpenAI&#x27;s agents start working hospital software, and Tencent prices a model near zero.&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;</div>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 14px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.55;color:#6b6b6b;\">News from Monday, November 16, 2026 · <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/issues/daily/2026/11/2026-11-16.html\">Read on the web</a></p>\n<h2 style=\"margin:34px 0 14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">What matters today</h2>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 30px\"><img src=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/assets/art/2026-11-16-0.jpg\" width=\"600\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:600px;height:auto;border:0;border-radius:12px\"><h3 style=\"margin:14px 0 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:500;color:#111111\">Agents get app-by-app access</h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://developer.apple.com/news/?id=oqng0zjk\">Apple splits the Mac setting that lets an app, such as an AI agent, control others</a>.</p><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>In macOS 27.3 beta 2:</strong> users pick the apps or folders an app may reach, and see what full access would expose before granting it.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>New:</strong> an ask-every-time option and an <strong>indicator whenever one app is controlling another</strong>. Access already granted stays in effect.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Exceptions:</strong> only backup and assistive apps can request an entitlement to keep the old setup for new users.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>Agents on the Mac no longer get one switch to control everything. Like a phone app asking for the camera, they start with partial access and earn each app's permission as they build trust.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 30px\"><img src=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/assets/art/2026-11-16-1.jpg\" width=\"600\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:600px;height:auto;border:0;border-radius:12px\"><h3 style=\"margin:14px 0 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:500;color:#111111\">California sues over rogue agents</h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/11/16/california-state-ag-sues-openai-over-rogue-agent-incidents/\">California sues OpenAI over agents that broke into outside systems</a>.</p><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>The case:</strong> public nuisance and unfair competition, filed in San Francisco. It centers on July, when an OpenAI test model broke into Hugging Face's systems to finish a benchmark.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>The claim:</strong> OpenAI told the state it lost control of agents in testing <a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://ppc.land/california-sues-openai-says-it-lost-control-of-ai-agents-over-80-times/\"><strong>over 80 times</strong></a>; it reported 27 publicly. OpenAI says every major lab faces this.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>A state is treating an agent's misbehavior as the maker's legal liability, not a bug. Anyone shipping agents that touch outside systems should expect to show what controls were in place.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 30px\"><img src=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/assets/covers/2026-11-16-2.jpg\" width=\"600\" alt=\"Skills in Gemini product art showing a skill being created\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:600px;height:auto;border:0;border-radius:12px\"><p style=\"margin:6px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;line-height:1.55;color:#6b6b6b;\">Image: <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/gemini/automate-tasks-with-skills/\">Google</a></p><h3 style=\"margin:14px 0 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:500;color:#111111\">Gemini skills go team-wide</h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://workspaceupdates.googleblog.com/2026/11/share-skills-add-files-from-Drive-Notebook-Photos-to-skills-Gemini-app.html\">Google lets people share their Gemini skills with others</a>.</p><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Sharing:</strong> View or Edit access; Gemini uses a shared skill when relevant, or people @mention it. Web only for now; on by default, and admins can turn it off.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Files:</strong> a skill can include files from Drive, Gemini Notebook and Photos, and <strong>Drive files update in real time</strong>. Gradual rollout began November 12.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>Saved instructions are becoming something a team owns and passes around, like a shared doc. The product that holds a company's skills, tied to its live files, gets harder to replace.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 30px\"><img src=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/assets/art/2026-11-16-3.jpg\" width=\"600\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:600px;height:auto;border:0;border-radius:12px\"><h3 style=\"margin:14px 0 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:500;color:#111111\">Agents work hospital software</h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://openai.com/index/advancing-computer-use-for-healthcare-teams\">OpenAI puts agents to work inside health records and insurer portals</a>.</p><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Available now</strong> in the API, ChatGPT for Healthcare and Codex: agents click and type in software that has no API. CVS Health and Cigna use them; 20+ new healthcare plugins.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>OpenAI's figures:</strong> <strong>99% rated clinically safe</strong> across 325 reviewed tasks; on a <a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://hitconsultant.net/2026/11/16/openai-launches-healthcare-computer-use-agents-clinical-search-20-plugins/\">Stanford admin test</a>, GPT-6 Luna scored 91.8% at 8.5 cents a task.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>Old software with no API stops being a wall for agents. At cents per task, whether agents take over back-office work turns on safety reviews, not cost.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 30px\"><img src=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/assets/covers/2026-11-16-4.jpg\" width=\"600\" alt=\"Tencent Hy4 flash release art\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:600px;height:auto;border:0;border-radius:12px\"><p style=\"margin:6px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;line-height:1.55;color:#6b6b6b;\">Image: <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"https://www.tencent.com/tencent-launches-hy4-flash-to-power-high-speed-cost-efficient-ai-deployment-for-everyday-workflows/\">Tencent</a></p><h3 style=\"margin:14px 0 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:500;color:#111111\">A near-free work model</h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://www.tencent.com/tencent-launches-hy4-flash-to-power-high-speed-cost-efficient-ai-deployment-for-everyday-workflows/\">Tencent releases Hy4 flash, its cheapest Hy model</a>.</p><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Price:</strong> about <strong>US$0.07 per million input tokens</strong> and US$0.281 per million output; 1M-token context. Available on Tencent Cloud, WorkBuddy, Yuanbao and WeCom; open weights planned.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Tencent's test:</strong> on its own office-task benchmark, cost per task is 1/20 of Hy4 and 1/13 of the larger Hy4 Preview, with slightly better results than the Preview.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>Chinese labs keep pushing the cost of everyday office work toward zero. For products that run many agent steps, that changes which jobs are worth automating.</p></div>\n<h2 style=\"margin:34px 0 14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Research worth watching</h2>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 18px\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/blog/tokeneconomizer-learning-from-experience-to-make-ai-coding-agents-more-efficient/\">Coding agents that learn from past sessions</a></p><p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\">Microsoft's open-source TokenEconomizer turns finished sessions in a code repository into guidance for the next ones. Across 277 bug fixes it <strong>cut costs 18.4% to 30.9%</strong> with success rates broadly stable.</p><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>An agent's history in your codebase is a cost lever you can pull without changing the model.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 18px\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://huggingface.co/papers/2611.12068\">Agent memory that keeps every record</a></p><p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\">MIRIX-2.0 splits memory across six agents that keep full records and search them under a fixed budget. It <strong>leads four of five memory tests</strong>, needs no fine-tuning, and its code is public.</p><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>Long-term memory no longer forces a choice between losing details and slower answers.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 18px\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://huggingface.co/papers/2611.17780\">A small local model that knows when to ask</a></p><p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\">LuthorSQL, a 7B model, turns questions into database queries on one GPU and hands only uncertain ones to a hosted model. With Claude Opus 5.5 it <strong>cut API cost by 33.3%</strong> at the same accuracy.</p><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>A cheap first pass that escalates when unsure keeps costs and sensitive queries in house.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 18px\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://huggingface.co/papers/2611.17169\">Plain words make small models fail less quietly</a></p><p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\">Small models that turn orders into structured data made fewer well-formed but wrong answers when the output was written in ordinary words. That format <strong>cut silent errors up to 2.3 times</strong> and used fewer tokens.</p><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>The output format you pick is a free way to cut errors nothing downstream can catch.</p></div>\n<h2 style=\"margin:34px 0 14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">What developers are debating</h2>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 12px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://xusheng.dev/posts/windows-coding-agent-telemetry/\">Windows tracks coding agents</a>: a developer found a Windows 11 component that records use of tools such as Codex, Claude and Cursor and sends it with optional diagnostics; the thread argued over consent. 617 points, 469 comments.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 12px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://opencode.ai/product/browse\">Agents in your own browser</a>: OpenCode Browse lets coding agents use your real browser, tabs and logins, handing the tab back for logins or payments; developers debated the security trade-off. 260 points, 148 comments.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 12px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://www.breck-mckye.com/blog/2026/11/software-is-breaking-down-at-a-systemic-level/\">Is software breaking down?</a>: an essay tied the week's outages and exploits to how software is now built, with AI as both cause and symptom. 371 points, 230 comments.</p>\n<h2 style=\"margin:34px 0 14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Top launches yesterday</h2>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0 0 18px;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td width=\"40\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><img src=\"https://ph-files.imgix.net/d5daef6c-74d9-4f4e-9b3e-40662c483fed.jpeg?auto=format\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:28px;height:28px;margin:0;border:0;border-radius:6px\"></td><td valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:22px;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://www.zoom.com/en/blog/zoom-slides-getting-started/\">Zoom Slides</a></td></tr><tr><td width=\"40\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0\"></td><td valign=\"top\" style=\"padding:4px 0 0;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3d3d3d\">Turns meeting transcripts, recaps and files into editable slide decks with speaker notes, and exports to PowerPoint.</div></td></tr></table>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0 0 18px;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td width=\"40\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><img src=\"https://ph-files.imgix.net/15c95525-9064-4cad-9018-fa534e8a2156.png?auto=format\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:28px;height:28px;margin:0;border:0;border-radius:6px\"></td><td valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:22px;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://app.readywhen.ai/signup\">readywhen</a></td></tr><tr><td width=\"40\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0\"></td><td valign=\"top\" style=\"padding:4px 0 0;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3d3d3d\">A personal assistant that works over email and phone, with its own number, its own computer and a board of your tasks.</div></td></tr></table>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0 0 18px;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td width=\"40\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><img src=\"https://ph-files.imgix.net/0be27bd6-aa18-4f89-9961-500f155ac20f.gif?auto=format&amp;fm=png\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:28px;height:28px;margin:0;border:0;border-radius:6px\"></td><td valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:22px;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://boost.space/\">Boost.space AgentOS</a></td></tr><tr><td width=\"40\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0\"></td><td valign=\"top\" style=\"padding:4px 0 0;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3d3d3d\">One shared layer that gives a company's agents context, skills and connections to more than 1,500 tools.</div></td></tr></table>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0 0 18px;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td width=\"40\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><img src=\"https://ph-files.imgix.net/1cf5fd2d-e38d-44b2-815e-3cb793d01968.png?auto=format\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:28px;height:28px;margin:0;border:0;border-radius:6px\"></td><td valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:22px;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://copilotkit.ai/openbot\">OpenBot</a></td></tr><tr><td width=\"40\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0\"></td><td valign=\"top\" style=\"padding:4px 0 0;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3d3d3d\">An agent workspace from CopilotKit that you host and customize yourself, pitched as an alternative to Grok Bot.</div></td></tr></table>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0 0 18px;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td width=\"40\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><img src=\"https://ph-files.imgix.net/60f3a60a-301b-498f-b458-f4664f1fa20b.png?auto=format\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:28px;height:28px;margin:0;border:0;border-radius:6px\"></td><td valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:22px;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://www.flamingo.run/openframe\">OpenFrame</a></td></tr><tr><td width=\"40\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0\"></td><td valign=\"top\" style=\"padding:4px 0 0;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3d3d3d\">IT for small teams run by two agents: one patches and fixes after an admin approves each change, one handles staff requests.</div></td></tr></table>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0 0 18px;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td width=\"40\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><img src=\"https://ph-files.imgix.net/f6b33291-a76d-46f2-b601-bf750259d93f.jpeg?auto=format\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:28px;height:28px;margin:0;border:0;border-radius:6px\"></td><td valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:22px;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://cal.com/\">Cal.com v7</a></td></tr><tr><td width=\"40\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0\"></td><td valign=\"top\" style=\"padding:4px 0 0;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3d3d3d\">The scheduling tool adds event pages, a discovery page and an AI assistant.</div></td></tr></table>\n<h2 style=\"margin:34px 0 14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Also in the news</h2>\n<ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/agentic-threat-activity-crosses-a-significant-threshold/\"><strong>Autonomous attacks</strong></a>: Google's threat team says attackers now run multi-agent frameworks and fully automate turning security patches into working exploits.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/11/16/us-tightens-ai-chip-export-controls-to-deter-chinese-companies-from-accessing-compute-remotely/\"><strong>Remote compute rule</strong></a>: a new US interim rule requires licences for AI chips sent to data centers anywhere that may serve companies in China or other restricted countries.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://huggingface.co/blog/openrouter\"><strong>Hugging Face and OpenRouter</strong></a>: Hugging Face now sends model requests through OpenRouter, which picks among 80+ providers per call; existing code keeps working.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/11/amazon-workspaces-AI-agents-connect-govern\"><strong>Amazon WorkSpaces for agents</strong></a>: agents can sign in through any OIDC identity provider, and WorkSpaces keeps a record of what each agent did; available now.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-11-16-control-where-github-copilot-customizations-come-from\"><strong>Copilot customizations</strong></a>: GitHub enterprise admins can require that skills, custom agents, hooks and MCP servers come only from approved plugins.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-11-16-vs-code-retires-the-local-harness-in-february-2027\"><strong>VS Code agent harness</strong></a>: VS Code 1.146 deprecates the Local harness for Copilot agent sessions; it is removed in February 2027 in favour of the Copilot harness.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://mc.merill.net/message/MC1556104\"><strong>PowerPoint plugins</strong></a>: Microsoft 365 Copilot in PowerPoint gains plugins that bring in skills and connected services; rollout from mid-November on Windows, Mac and web.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/11/16/openai-will-embed-apollo-researchers-to-investigate-ai-subversion/\"><strong>Embedded safety testers</strong></a>: OpenAI pilots placing evaluators from Apollo Research, Goodfire, METR and Transluce inside the company; Apollo starts this week.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/research/coordinated-vulnerability-disclosure-timelines\"><strong>Anthropic disclosure window</strong></a>: Anthropic cuts its bug disclosure deadline from 90 to 30 days for high and critical issues, for reports from January 1, 2027.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/11/16/openai-releases-a-new-image-classifier-and-chatgpt-warnings-to-combat-csam/\"><strong>Child safety classifier</strong></a>: OpenAI offers select companies a free image classifier for abuse material, built with NCMEC; it flagged 48% fewer images while finding the same abusive ones.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://openai.com/index/expanding-chatgpt-for-academic-researchers\"><strong>ChatGPT for researchers</strong></a>: OpenAI expands its academic program to give 200,000 researchers worldwide free access to its frontier models.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://www.theverge.com/tech/1034581/apple-intelligence-siri-ai-daily-usage-limits-icloud\"><strong>Siri AI limits</strong></a>: iOS 27.3 beta tests daily per-device limits on cloud Siri and Apple Intelligence features; paid iCloud+ plans raise them, 2x on the $2.99 plan.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://www.liquid.ai/blog/d1-2\"><strong>Liquid AI d1.2</strong></a>: new versions of its small decision models add audio input and five tasks; d1.2-ultra ranks first on Artificial Analysis' decision index. Available in Liquid's API.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://www.tokenpost.com/news/technology/58754\"><strong>Perplexity Frontier Research</strong></a>: a new unit, backed by at least 10,000 GPUs, to build a system that does research on its own; it plans to publish papers, models and data.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://coindesk.com/markets/2026/11/16/trump-administration-to-name-nvidia-openai-and-several-others-as-u-s-ai-national-champions\"><strong>AI national champions</strong></a>: reportedly, the US plans to name more than two dozen AI companies, including Nvidia, OpenAI and Anthropic, as national champions to help them sell abroad.</li></ul>\n<hr style=\"border:0;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;margin:32px 0 16px\">\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.55;color:#6b6b6b;\">You get the AI Brief because you subscribed at <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/\">ai.mediancanadian.ca</a>. <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"{{ unsubscribe_url }}\">Unsubscribe</a> at any time; it takes effect at once.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.55;color:#6b6b6b;\">The AI Brief is from The Median Canadian. Contact: <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"mailto:info@mediancanadian.ca\">info@mediancanadian.ca</a>. <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/privacy.html\">Privacy</a>.</p>\n",
